The Massachusetts Tenth Middlesex State Representative District includes portions of Newton, Waltham, and Watertown, covering an area of 5 square miles with a population of 43,110. The district is currently represented by incumbent John J. Lawn, Jr. (D-Watertown), who has held the seat since winning a special election in 2011 and has run unopposed in most recent elections.


